BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Snakefest 2026\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260718T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260718T170000
UID:475145b3d8d4ca173262c53598939430@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Come join the Brown County State Park naturalists\, O&#39\;Ban
 non Woods State Park naturalists\, and the Hoosier Herptological Society f
 or an exciting Saturday! We have walk up displays of reptiles all day\, wi
 th opportunities for learning\, petting\, and pictures! Special presentati
 ons occur at the top of every hour. We also have some snake arts and craft
 s to take with you! 11am: Earth&#39\;s Most Venomous Snakes 12pm: Snake Me
 et and Greet 1pm: Searching for Hidden Herps 2pm: Timber! Understanding th
 e Timber Rattlesnake 3pm: Snakes of Indiana 4pm: Rattlesnake Walk 5pm: Sna
 ke Meet and Greet
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mothing in Indiana\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260725T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260725T230000
UID:491dd54e89d059f890500cc818459e1e@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Moths may conjure images of drab and brown insects fluttering 
 at our porch lights\, but with over 2\,300 species recorded in the state\,
  there&rsquo\;s much to learn about these mostly-nocturnal fliers. We&rsqu
 o\;ll have a few lights set up to attract moths to a white sheet so we can
  view the stunning diversity of these little gems. This is an excellent pr
 ogram for families\, and children of all ages are encouraged to attend. Br
 ing a flashlight for best viewing of moths on the sheet.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, Friends' Shelter\, 1405
  S.R. 46 W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
